/-!
# Fixed matrices for the cubic principal series

These definitions encode the two monomial generators and the commuting
nilpotent candidate extracted from the retained GAP diagnostic. No matrix
identity or comparison with the actual SU₃(5) induction is asserted here.
The candidate is the off-diagonal orbital matrix plus the identity.

The diagnostic uses right row actions. `generatorMatrix` and
`nilpotentMatrix` transpose after coefficient specialization. A coordinate
comparison must match these with the inverse group actors and the inverse
of the original Borel character; transposition alone does not suffice.

Entries are encoded in base four: 0, 1, ω, 1+ω have codes 0, 1, 2, 3.
The generator and original flag came from
`Scratch/SU3Cubic/{gap_flag_data.g,twisted_flag_diagnostic.g}` in retained
workspace `089e6b32637547ea996eba0fc78397ec`. The extraction and orbital
reconstruction are preserved in this module's `source/` directory.
Source motivation: Guralnick–Malle, Proposition 4.3, p.10.
-/

